From: Vertex Shot Timer <vertex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm: mach-sstar: infinity6e: drive PAD_GPIO13 as power-hold

This board latches its own power rail: after the button is released the SoC has
to keep PAD_GPIO13 high or the board dies mid-boot.  No kernel code did that,
so power was held only for as long as the button was physically down.

Assert the pad from a late_initcall with the same gpiolib entry point
mstar_usb_vbus_control() uses a few hundred lines up in this file.
gpio_request() on this SoC also switches the pad into GPIO mode
(camdriver_gpio_request -> MDrv_GPIO_Pad_Set -> HalPadSetVal(idx,
PINMUX_FOR_GPIO_MODE)), so the level sticks whatever the padmux schematic last
assigned to the pad, and the boot no longer depends on the U-Boot environment
having been edited to add "gpio output 112 1" to bootcmd.

late_initcall is required rather than cosmetic.  The sstar,gpio chip is
registered by camdriver_gpio_init() at postcore_initcall
(drivers/sstar/gpio/mdrv_gpio_io.c), while .init_machine is reached from
arch_initcall(customize_machine) in arch/arm/kernel/setup.c -- requesting a GPIO
from there races chip registration and silently fails.  late_initcall is past
device_initcall, so the chip is always there.

If the request ever fails the boot still continues: a board whose power hold
cannot be asserted is a board that needs the button held down, not one that
should hang before the console.

--- a/arch/arm/mach-sstar/infinity6e/soc.c	2026-10-16 16:42:50.993644523 +0700
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sstar/infinity6e/soc.c	2026-10-16 16:46:08.856505843 +0700
@@ -574,6 +574,30 @@
 
 
 
+/*
+ * The board latches its own power on PAD_GPIO13: nothing keeps the rail up
+ * once the button is released unless the SoC drives this pad itself.  U-Boot
+ * does it from bootcmd; the padmux schematic used to take the pad back for
+ * PWM5 at postcore_initcall, which is what the companion patch removes.
+ *
+ * late_initcall because gpio_request() needs the sstar,gpio chip, registered by
+ * camdriver_gpio_init() at postcore_initcall.  .init_machine runs earlier, from
+ * arch_initcall(customize_machine), and would race it.
+ */
+static int __init mstar_power_hold_init(void)
+{
+    if (gpio_request(PAD_GPIO13, "power-hold") < 0) {
+        pr_err("power-hold: cannot request PAD_GPIO13\n");
+        return -EINVAL;
+    }
+
+    gpio_direction_output(PAD_GPIO13, 1);
+    pr_info("power-hold: PAD_GPIO13 driven high\n");
+
+    return 0;
+}
+late_initcall(mstar_power_hold_init);
+
 extern void mstar_create_MIU_node(void);
 extern int mstar_pm_init(void);
 extern void init_proc_zen(void);
